Security Notes
Do not store Azure passwords or credentials in the PowerShell script.
Use Azure interactive authentication or an approved service principal / managed identity.
Do not commit sensitive authentication information to source-control repositories.
Ensure the input CSV does not contain unnecessary sensitive information.
Follow your organization's Azure RBAC and security policies.
Summary

This script provides a simple way to generate a consolidated Azure VNET inventory across multiple subscriptions from a CSV subscription list.

The resulting report can be used for:

Network inventory
IP address management
Azure network audits
Migration planning
Network documentation
Compliance reporting
VNET and subnet analysis

Input: subscriptions.csv

Output: Azure-VNET-Inventory.csv

Authentication: Connect-AzAccount

Primary Azure cmdlets:

Connect-AzAccount
Set-AzContext
Get-AzVirtualNetwork
